  "Question": "Given the circle \\(x^2+y^2=25\\) and the line \\(x=5\\), what is the distance from the center of the circle to the line?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "5",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The circle has center \\(O=(0,0)\\) and radius \\(5\\). Since \\(x=5\\) is vertical, the perpendicular from \\(O\\) meets the line at \\(H=(5,0)\\), giving distance \\(OH=5-0=5\\). This equals the radius, so the line is tangent to the circle; the requested distance is \\(5\\).",
